      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe decode allocation path calls `get_num_new_pages` on CPU tensors for every scheduling step. The existing `.int().sum()` sequence copies the boolean mask to int32 before reducing it. This removes that unnecessary dtype conversion from the host-side hot path.\n\nRelated to #24922.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Replace the decode-path `.int().sum()` with `torch.count_nonzero`.\n- Correct the helper return annotation to `int`.\n- Add a regression test that verifies the page count and absence of `aten._to_copy`.\n- Add a focused host-side microbenchmark comparing the legacy and current implementations.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThis does not change model outputs. The unit test covers page-boundary counting and passes:\n\n`python test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_num_new_pages.py`\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nCommand:\n\n`python benchmark/scheduler/bench_num_new_pages.py --iterations 5000 --repeats 5`\n\nWSL2, PyTorch 2.10.0+xpu, CPU host path:\n\n| Batch | Legacy (us) | Current (us) | Helper speedup |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 4.670 | 3.094 | 1.51x |\n| 8 | 4.728 | 3.195 | 1.48x |\n| 32 | 4.935 | 3.315 | 1.49x |\n| 128 | 4.985 | 3.545 | 1.41x |\n\nThe local Intel XPU runtime currently reports zero devices, so these results only measure the CPU helper. End-to-end GPU performance has not been measured, and this PR does not claim a GPU performance improvement.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format checks pass for all changed files.\n- [x] Added a registered CPU/XPU unit test.\n- [x] Documentation is not needed for this internal helper change.\n- [x] Included the available focused benchmark and its GPU-validation limitation.\n- [x] Followed the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38231355869](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231355869)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38231355300](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231355300)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38231355777](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231355777)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
